==Collaboration Exclusive==
During the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]], when The 9th Angel Strikes! is available, the cat is replaced with Gendo Ikari, who has some unique lines:
*Target is closing in. You will defeat it.
*[[The 9th Angel (Enemy)|EVA 03]] is a total loss. Designate it the 9th Angel.
*Our future depends on defeating the [[:Category:EVA Angel Enemies|Angels]].
*Get in the EVA, or get out of here.
*All personnel to battle stations.
*If this doesn't work, there's always the Cats.

When [[EVA Unit-13 Strikes!]] is available, Gendo (wearing a futuristic red visor instead of glasses) says these lines instead:
*[[Unit-13's False Evolution|Evangelion Unit 13]]. You will pilot it.
*All the tools have been gathered.
*We are rewriting Seele's scenario. All Cats are simply means to that end.

During the [[World Trigger Collaboration Event]], the cat is replaced with Shiori Usami, who says these lines instead:
*Increase the population of glasses-wearers in the Cat Army!
*I'll create a space for training. Activate Training Room 222!
*The training room is set to virtual mode, so you can let loose and fight hard.

==Switch Exclusive==
On the Nintendo Switch version, there are some splash text that is exclusive to this version.

*In VS mode, the best path to Victory is to know as much about each Cat's Traits and Abilities as you can!
*You can change enemy Traits with the Trait Cannon in VS mode! Then, send in your Trait-targeting specialist Cats to fight!
*Choosing Level Adjust at the pre-battle menu will set all Cats to the same power level! Even if their level changes, your Cats' appearance will stay the same!
*Choosing Stage Size at the pre-battle menu will change the space you have to fight!
*Pressing down on the stick at the Unit Info screen will let you check the abilities the current unit has.
*If a Unit has an evolved form unlocked, you can press the Y Button to change between the first and second forms!
*Choosing Time Limit at the pre-battle menu will end the battle after a set amount of time! Set a longer time if you want a relaxed showdown!
*Cannon Targeting's biggest damage will be directed at the dead center of the shot!
*Touch this speech bubble for another new bit of useful advice! Everything is learning!
*Choosing Team Limits at the pre-battle menu will let players use only certain types of Cats. Just gotta be flexible and roll with the punches to win!
*If one of your Cats falls in battle, your Power Gauge will go down! Victory comes from careful planning!
*You can decide the rules of your VS battle before the fight begins!
*You can use the Trait Cannon to attack the Enemy base too! Wait for the right moment before firing!
*Fine-tune your battle crew by copying Cat lineups from any Formation to a new one!

==Trivia==
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], the line, "The main ingredient for a Cat… is happiness," more closely translates to "Half of a Cat is made out of kindness," which is phrased almost identically to the tagline of the painkiller [[wikipedia:ja:バファリン|Bufferin]].
*"Stay hungry. Stay foolish," is a famous quote from entrepreneur and co-founder of Apple [[wikipedia:Steve Jobs|Steve Jobs]].
*In the [[Catclaw Dojo]] splash text, ''consquences'' is spelt incorrectly. It should be written as ''consequences''.
*"GOTTA CATCH 'EM ALL!" is the slogan of the [[wikipedia:Pokémon|''Pokémon'']] franchise.
*Prior to [[Version 10.7 Update|Version 10.7]], the "Zombie Outbreak in <chapter>!" splash test said, "Go there now?" at the end of the splash with the options "yes" and "no".
*"I heard a guy at the bus stop say that the Future has a lot of treasure that can make you strong against Aliens!" may be an indirect reference to [[Cyberhorn]]'s English description, which claims he was meant to appear in Chapter 1, but was too slow to catch the bus.
